":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges. O(m)."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/GraphProtocols-MutableDirectedGraph-Extensions","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/graphprotocols-mutabledirectedgraph-extensions","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Members other modules add to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Extensions to MutableDirectedGraph"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph/stronglyConnectedComponents()":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The strongly connected components: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" are together when each reaches the other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"along source → hyperedge → target steps (Gallo et al.‘s “connected”: a path in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence graph). They are the strong components of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidenceGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" restricted to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, ordered by least vertex index, each in index order. Mutual B-connection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(SimpleDirectedHypergraphs.jl’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"get_strongly_connected_components"},{"type":"text","text":") is a different,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finer relation."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph\/stronglyConnectedComponents()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","t